  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I actually go about finding an IB tutor in Tumkur?", answer: "Tell us the essentials first: the Bengaluru school or online provider your child is registered with, or the board they are moving away from, plus the subject, level and exam session, since Tumkur has no school of its own teaching the IB. From there we put forward tutors with recent, matching experience and land on a time that suits your household, with an online trial class happening before anything is finalised." },
    { question: "Is there truly no school inside Tumkur offering IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Truly none, and that holds even for the handful of schools that market themselves as 'International.' Look past the name and the syllabus underneath is CBSE. A family after the real thing sends a child to a school in Bengaluru, about 70 kilometres off, or opts for an accredited online international school while staying put in Tumkur." },
    { question: "Will a tutor actually come to our home in Tumkur?", answer: "No, not in Tumkur. A tutor physically visiting a family is offered only within Gurugram and a slice of Delhi NCR, and that arrangement simply does not extend anywhere else, Tumkur among them. Instead, a Tumkur family gets a full live session, one to one over video with the screen shared both ways, run by a tutor who could be based anywhere in India. The tuition is real and taken from home; only the doorstep visit is missing." },
    { question: "Which schools should a Tumkur family actually look at for IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Two options run the IB Diploma outright, Canadian International School in Bengaluru and The International School Bangalore, while Stonehill International School teaches the entire IB continuum and offers both day and boarding places. Each sits somewhere between 70 and 80 kilometres from Tumkur, near enough to consider a daily run and far enough that boarding usually wins out in the end." },
    { question: "What is the actual cost picture for a Tumkur family hiring an IB or IGCSE tutor?", answer: "The number moves with the level being taught, how hard that subject is to staff, the length of each session and how recently a tutor has handled that precise syllabus, and we lay it out clearly before any trial begins. A tutor's own city never factors in, since every lesson happens over the same video link regardless." },
    { question: "Does the free trial class come with any strings attached?", answer: "None. A tutor runs one full class on a real topic straight from your child's syllabus, at zero cost and zero obligation to book anything further. Only afterward does that tutor outline a first month's plan, leaving the choice to continue, adjust, or walk away entirely in your hands." },
    { question: "Can a tutor write part of my child's IB Internal Assessment?", answer: "No, though plenty of legitimate help sits short of that line: narrowing down a workable research question, explaining what a criterion is actually rewarding, checking whether a data-collection method makes sense, and giving frank feedback on a draft. Anything that puts a tutor's own writing into the final submission counts as an integrity violation and is declined outright, every time." },
    { question: "Which specific IB Diploma subjects can a Tumkur family get help with?", answer: "Both Maths options, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management and English A account for most of what Tumkur families ask about, spanning the standard subject groups, with Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay support available for whatever a student is working on." },
    { question: "Is support available for MYP and PYP students too, or only the Diploma?", answer: "The full continuum is covered. At MYP level, the usual focus is helping a student move beyond describing a topic into properly analysing it, particularly in science subjects, alongside sustained help with the Year 5 Personal Project. PYP-age children work on reading, writing and early number confidence in short sessions built around a family's own timetable." },
    { question: "With no IB or IGCSE school anywhere nearby, can online tutoring genuinely deliver?", answer: "It can, largely because that absence is exactly the problem online tutoring solves: Tumkur simply has no specialist on hand for something like IB Chemistry HL or IGCSE Additional Mathematics. Screen sharing, worked examples and a tutor talking through a problem step by step do not need anyone in the room to work, while reaching specialists well beyond whatever a short local list could offer." },
    { question: "What vetting does a tutor go through before being matched to a family here?", answer: "Qualifications, recent hands-on experience teaching the exact subject and level, and a sensible approach to guiding coursework all get checked before a name is ever proposed. Given that Tumkur has no local pool of such tutors to fall back on, current experience is weighted well above a generic profile, and the trial class is where a family confirms that judgement for themselves." },
    { question: "Is there an ideal point to begin IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Starting alongside the course itself works best, Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma, since it leaves time to shore up fundamentals before internal exams, coursework deadlines and predicted grades all converge. Even a late start, in the final year or right after settling into a Bengaluru school, can still produce real gains by targeting the highest-value topics and past papers." },
    { question: "My child is moving off the Karnataka State Board or CBSE, usually while joining a school in Bengaluru. Does tutoring help with that transition?", answer: "It does, and this particular situation comes up often enough from Tumkur to be nearly routine. Content rarely trips a switching student up; exam language does, understanding precisely what a word like 'evaluate' or 'analyse' demands, alongside fresh habits for Internal Assessment and coursework planning. Beginning the summer before both changes land at once gives that adjustment the best chance of going smoothly." },
    { question: "Is it possible to schedule around a heavy commute or a parent's own travel to Bengaluru?", answer: "Yes, and it is one of the more common requests from this city specifically. Weekday evenings after the day's travel, weekend slots, or whatever window a family's week actually has tend to work best, and revision blocks get planned around leave taken for exams and breaks like Ugadi or Dasara rather than assuming a fixed routine." },
    { question: "What is the process if a tutor turns out to be the wrong fit?", answer: "Raise it, and a replacement gets sourced. Regular check-ins with families every few weeks exist specifically to surface this kind of issue early rather than letting a child struggle through it. No long contract sits behind any of this, so pausing or stopping is possible at any time without cost." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram have any formal tie to a Bengaluru school, Tumkur University, or exam boards like the IB and Cambridge?", answer: "None at all. This is an independent service, unconnected to any school in Bengaluru or Tumkur, to Tumkur University or Siddaganga Institute of Technology, or to the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education and Pearson Edexcel. Schools mentioned on this page simply show where families actually study, and tutors work to that school's calendar and the relevant board's published syllabus, nothing more." },
  ],

